    "overview": {
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "signs-you-need-a-complete-engine-replacement",
          "title": "Signs You Need a Complete Engine Replacement",
          "description": "Before committing to a supply-and-fit engine replacement, check if your symptoms indicate terminal failure:",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "🔊 Deep knocking or rumbling from engine"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Rod bearing or main bearing failure - bottom-end damage is usually terminal."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "❌ Replace"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "🛑 Complete engine seizure"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Catastrophic internal failure - no oil pressure, rod through block - engine is scrap."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "❌ Replace"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "⛓️ Snapped timing belt/chain on interference engine"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Valves have hit pistons - extensive damage. Repair often costs more than replacement."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "❌ Replace"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "🔄 Crankshaft bearing failure"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Spun bearing, damaged crankshaft, debris in oil system - destroys the block."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "❌ Replace"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "🌡️ Persistent overheating with oil contamination"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Head gasket failure, cracked block or cylinder head - may be repairable if caught early."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "⚠️ Evaluate"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "⚙️ Metal shavings in oil"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Internal wear - bearings, rings, cylinder bores - internal damage is widespread."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "❌ Replace"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "\"Most of the engines we replace are beyond economic repair. When you're looking at a snapped timing chain, a spun bearing, or a seized engine, the cost of repair often exceeds the cost of replacement - and you still don't know what else is damaged inside. Supply-and-fit gives you a clean slate.\""
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "- UK Engine Specialist Interview #11 [EM-INTERVIEW]"
            }
          ],
          "links": [],
          "source": {
            "sectionId": "signs-you-need-a-complete-engine-replacement",
            "order": 0
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "included": {
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "what-s-included-in-supply-and-fit",
          "title": "What's Included in Supply and Fit",
          "description": "When you choose a supply-and-fit service, you're getting a complete turnkey solution - not just a bare engine.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": "h3",
              "id": "",
              "text": "What's Included"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Engine supply: Used, reconditioned, rebuilt, or remanufactured unit.",
                "Removal of old engine: Professional dismantling and removal.",
                "Fitting replacement unit: Professional installation to factory specs.",
                "New consumables: Engine oil, coolant, and oil filter replaced.",
                "Basic gaskets & seals: Replaced as part of installation.",
                "Testing & sign-off: Oil pressure, compression, and leak checks.",
                "Warranty: Parts & labour warranty (6-24 months depending on unit).",
                "Disposal of old unit: Environmentally compliant scrapping."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": "h3",
              "id": "",
              "text": "What's NOT Included (Hidden Costs to Watch For)"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Clutch & DMF: £400-£1,000 extra (manuals - labour saved if done now).",
                "Water pump / thermostat: £100-£300 extra (recommended precaution).",
                "Air-con regas: £50-£150 extra after refrigerant discharge.",
                "Ancillary parts: Alternator, starter, turbo if existing are worn (£200-£1,000+).",
                "Unforeseen repairs: Seized bolts, corroded pipes discovered during swap.",
                "Vehicle recovery: £100-£300+ extra if car is non-drivable."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "links": [],
          "source": {
            "sectionId": "what-s-included-in-supply-and-fit",
            "order": 1
          }
        }
      ]
    },
