    "faq": {
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "frequently-asked-questions",
          "title": "Frequently Asked Questions",
          "description": "Common questions about engine supply and fit services.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "cards",
              "cards": [
                {
                  "title": "How much does supply and fit cost?",
                  "text": "How much does supply and fit cost? Supply-and-fit costs vary by condition type: Used £2,500-£4,500, Reconditioned £3,500-£5,500, Rebuilt £4,500-£7,500, Remanufactured £5,500-£9,000. Labour is the biggest variable - regional rates range from £65-£160/hr.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "How much does supply and fit cost? Supply-and-fit costs vary by condition type: Used £2,500-£4,500, Reconditioned £3,500-£5,500, Rebuilt £4,500-£7,500, Remanufactured £5,500-£9,000. Labour is the biggest variable - regional rates range from £65-£160/hr."
                },
                {
                  "title": "What's included in the fitting cost?",
                  "text": "What's included in the fitting cost? Fitting typically includes: removal of the old engine, installation of the replacement engine, new consumables (oil, coolant, filters), basic gaskets and seals, post-installation testing, and disposal of the old engine. Always get a written breakdown.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "What's included in the fitting cost? Fitting typically includes: removal of the old engine, installation of the replacement engine, new consumables (oil, coolant, filters), basic gaskets and seals, post-installation testing, and disposal of the old engine. Always get a written breakdown."
                },
                {
                  "title": "How long does engine replacement take?",
                  "text": "How long does engine replacement take? The average timeline from quote request to completion is 5.2 days [EM-VERIFIED]. Labour typically takes 8-15 hours depending on engine type and vehicle complexity.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "How long does engine replacement take? The average timeline from quote request to completion is 5.2 days [EM-VERIFIED]. Labour typically takes 8-15 hours depending on engine type and vehicle complexity."
                },
                {
                  "title": "What warranty comes with supply and fit?",
                  "text": "What warranty comes with supply and fit? The warranty depends on the condition type: Used 1-6 months (parts only), Reconditioned 6-12 months (parts & labour), Rebuilt 12-24 months (parts & labour), Remanufactured 12-24 months (parts & labour).",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "What warranty comes with supply and fit? The warranty depends on the condition type: Used 1-6 months (parts only), Reconditioned 6-12 months (parts & labour), Rebuilt 12-24 months (parts & labour), Remanufactured 12-24 months (parts & labour)."
                },
                {
                  "title": "Do you offer vehicle recovery?",
                  "text": "Do you offer vehicle recovery? Some suppliers offer recovery as part of the service. If not, you can arrange independent recovery or use your breakdown cover. We recommend confirming recovery options when you get your quotes.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "Do you offer vehicle recovery? Some suppliers offer recovery as part of the service. If not, you can arrange independent recovery or use your breakdown cover. We recommend confirming recovery options when you get your quotes."
                },
                {
                  "title": "Can I choose my own garage?",
                  "text": "Can I choose my own garage? If you choose supply-only, you can use any garage. If you choose supply-and-fit, the supplier will arrange fitting with one of their partner garages.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "Can I choose my own garage? If you choose supply-only, you can use any garage. If you choose supply-and-fit, the supplier will arrange fitting with one of their partner garages."
                },
                {
                  "title": "What if I already have my own garage?",
                  "text": "What if I already have my own garage? You can choose supply-only and have the engine delivered to your chosen garage. The supplier will provide the engine; your garage handles the fitting.",
                  "highlight": "",
